$DATUM 862589-30-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The crude catalyst (50.0 mg, 0.045 mmol) was dissolved in 0.5 mL of 1M
BH3-THF (0.5mmol, stabilized with 0.005 NaBH4) in THF (2 equiv BH3) under
argon atmosphere at room temperature. Then a solution of acetophenone
(30.0 mg, 0.25 mmol) in 1 mL of dry THF was added slowly over a period of
30 min. The reaction mixture was stirred for additional 30 minutes to
complete. Then it was quenched with 1.0 mL of MeOH, followed by the
additionof 1 mL of H2O which induced the instant precipitation of
fluorous compounds. This heterogeneous mixture was loaded on and filtered
through fluorous silica gel (FluoroFlashTM) followed by MeOH-water 1:1
(4X2.5 mL) washing to elute all nonfluorous products. Then the combined
filtrates were concentrated in vacuo to remove organic solvents and the
chiralsecunder alcohol was extracted with chloroform (3X5 mL). The
combined organic phases was dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated in vacuo.
Yield. 99% information not present
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Recoverable Fluorous CBS Methodology for Asymmetric Reduction of Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dalicsek, Zoltan; Pollreisz, Ferenc; Goemoery, Agnes; Soos, Tibor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(15), 3243-3246

