$DATUM 862589-19-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The precatalyst (54.50 mg, 0.05 mmol) was dissolved, in 1 mL of 1M
BH3-THF (1 mmol, nonstabilized) in THF (2 equiv BH3).under argon
atmosphere at room temperature and stirred for one hour. Then a solution
of ketone (0.5 mmol) in 1 mL of dry THF was added slowly over a period of
one hour. The reaction mixture was stirred for additional 30 minutes to
complete. Then it was cooled to 0 °C and quenched with 0.5 mL of MeOH.
Addition of 2.5 mL of water to the reaction mixture induced the instant
precipitation of precatalyst . This heterogeneous mixture was loaded on
and filtered through fluorous silica gel (FluoroFlashTM) followed by
acetonitrile-water 1:1(4X2.5 mL) washing to elute all nonfluorous
products. Then the combined filtrates were concentrated in vacuo to
remove organic solvents and the chiral secunder alcohol was extracted
with chloroform (3X5 mL). The combined organic phases was dried over
Na2SO4and evaporated in vacuo to give product. Yield. 99%. 1H-NMR (200
MHz, CDCl3) 7.40-7.25 (m, 5H, ArH), 4.88 (q, J= 6.3 Hz, 1H, CHOH), 2.10
(br s, 1H, OH), 1.49 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H, CH3CH); 13C-NMR (50MHz, CD3Cl)
145.9 (C), 128.6 (CH), 127.6 (CH), 125.5 (CH), 70.5 (CH), 25.2 (CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
