$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Asymmetric Reduction of Acetophenone with Catalyst 2; Typical Procedure.
A 100 mL, flame-dried, two-necked, round-bottomed flask equipped with a
magnetic stirrer bar was charged with catalyst 2 (0.66 mmol) and anhyd
THF (4 mL). PhCOMe (2 mmol, 0.22 mL) was then added under argon from a
syringe. Subsequently, BH3•THF (2.4 mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added dropwise
with the aid of a syringe pump at a rate of 1 mL/h, and the solution was
then stirred at r.t. under argon for 18 h. When the reaction was
complete, the mixture was hydrolyzed by addition of MeOH (5 mL) and 1 M
aq HCl (5 mL). Workup as described in ref. 14 gave enantiomerically
enriched 1-phenylethanol as a colorless oil; yield: 0.19 g (78%).
(1S)-1-Phenylethanol (4a) 16. ee 46% (catalyst B). HPLC: Lux Cellulose-1,
hexane-i-PrOH (98:2); flow rate: 1.0 mL/min, λ = 254 nm; tR (R) = 18.5
min, tR (S) = 24.7 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 46% ee, optimization study, optimized on reagent and
catalyst loading
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic asymmetric reduction of prochiral ketones with chiral β-amino
alcohol N-boranes and the corresponding tris(oxazaborolidine)borazines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pinaka, Afroditi; Dimotikali, Dimitra; Chankvetadze, Bezhan;
Papadopoulos, Kyriakos; Vougioukalakis, Georgios C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2013), 24(18), 2401-2406

