$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Quinone alcohol 35: To a stirred solution of tricyclic aldehyde 19a (3.04
g, 8.12 mmol) in MeOH (50 mL) was added NaBH4 (368 mg, 9.74 mmol) at 0
°C. The resulting mixture was stirred at that temperature for 15 min
before it was quenched with saturated aq. NH4Cl (100 mL) and extracted
with EtOAc (3 × 100 mL). The combined organic phases were washed with
brine (100 mL), dried over anhydrous MgSO4, and filtered. The solvent was
removed under vacuum, and the residue was purified by flash column
chromatography with EtOAc/petroleum ether (1:10) to give the product.
corresponding alcohol, yield: (2.90 g, 95%) as a yellow oil.
