$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Potassium 4-Hydroxyethylphenyltrifluoroborate
(3a). 4- Acetylphenylboronic acid (1.00 g, 6.10 mmol) was dissolved in
anhyd EtOH (5.0 mL) and cooled 0 °C with an ice/water bath. NaBH4 (579
mg, 15.2 mmol) was added all at once as a solid. After stirring for 16 h,
additional EtOH (5.0 mL) was added and the mixture was stirred for 4 h.
The soln was cooled to 0 °C and treated with 1N HCl (30 mL, 30 mmol). The
mixture was then extracted with EtOAc (3 X 15 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and
concentrated. The crude boronic acid was then dissolved in MeOH (10 mL)
and cooled to 0 °C. Satd aq KHF2 (6.8 mL, 31 mmol) was added dropwise via
syringe. The mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 2 h, concentrated, and
placed under high-vacuum (0.001 Torr) for 3 h. The dried solids were
triturated with hot acetone (3 X 20 mL) and filtered to remove
inorganicsalts. The resulting filtrate was concentrated and Et2O was
added to precipitate a white solid (1.15 g, 83%): Potassium
3-(1-Hydroxyethyl)phenyltrifluoroborate (3b). This compound was
synthesized from 3-acetylphenyltrifluoroborate according to the procedure
described for 3a to give a white crystalline solid (1.17 g, 90% yield):
mp 189-192 °C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.28 (s, 1H), 7.16-7.14 (m,
1H), 7.02-6.99 (m, 2H), 4.81 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 4.62-4.57 (m, 1H), 1.27
(d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 144.5, 129.7, 128.6,
125.8, 122.0, 68.9, 26.1; 11B NMR (128 MHz, DMSO-d6) 2.87 (br s); 19F NMR
(471 MHz, DMSO-d6) -139.3 (m); IR (KBr) 3600, 3539, 2982, 2875, 1420
cm-1; HRMS calcd. for C8H9BF3O [M-K]- 189.0698, found 189.0707.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oxidation of Hydroxyl-Substituted Organotrifluoroborates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Molander, Gary A.; Petrillo, Daniel E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(30), 9634-9635

