$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R)-2-Bromo-3-methylcyclohex-2-en-1-ol (10) To a solution of
α,α-diphenyl-L-prolinol (240 mg, 0.95 mmol) in THF (37 mL) was added
B(OMe)3 (0.13 mL, 1.14 mmol). The solution was stirred at rt for 70 min
and cooled to -5 ºC. BH3·NEt2Ph (3.72 mL, 20.9 mmol) was added to the
solution drop wise over 5 min. After the addition, the solution was
stirred at -5 ºC for 50 min. A solution of enone 9 (3.59 g, 19.0 mmol) in
THF (93 mL) was added slowly over 6 h at -5 ºC. After the addition, the
solution was stirred at -5 ºC for 18 h and the remaining hydride was
quenched by addition of MeOH (several drops). The solution was diluted
with 1 N HCl and extracted with EtOAc twice. The combined organic phases
were washed with saturated NaHCO3 and brine successively, dried over
MgSO4, and concentrated to leave an oil, which was purified by
chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc), Allylic alcohol 10 (3.26 g,
90%) as a white needle crystals, which were 98% ee as determined by
chiral HPLC. The ee of 10 was improved to 99.1% by recrystallization from
hexane with 89% recovery. Mp 43.4-44.3 ºC (lit.S2 43.3-46.3 ºC); [α]D 21
+101 (c 1.10, CHCl3) (lit.S2 78.7º, 77% ee, c 5.64, CHCl3); IR (neat)
3275, 1655, 973 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.58-1.69 (m, 1H),
1.72-1.94 (m, 3H), 1.84 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 3H), 2.03-2.19 (m, 2H), 2.18 (d,
J = 3.6 Hz, 1H), 4.23-4.30 (m, 1H); 13C-APT NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 18.2
(-), 23.5 (+), 32.0 (-), 33.3 (-), 71.0 (+), 122.5 (-), 137.1 (-).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on catalyst, optimized on
reagent, optimized on temperature, optimized on time, R-isomer ee:98%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Synthesis of Anastrephin via the Allylic Substitution for
Quaternary Carbon Construction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wada, Kyohei; Sakai, Masahiro; Kawashima, Hidehisa; Ogawa, Narihito;
Kobayashi, Yuichi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2016), 27(9), 1428-1432

