$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Keto diol 9. To a solution of aldehyde 8 (1.70 g, 3.64 mmol) in MeOH (10
mL) was added NaBH4 (69 mg, 1.82 mmol) at 0°C. After 30 min, the reaction
mixture was treated with saturated NH4Cl (5 mL). The aqueous layer was
extracted with Et2O (20 mL × 3). The combined extracts were washed with
brine (10 mL), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
dissolved in THF (5 mL) and a solution of tetra-n-butylammonium fluoride
(1M in THF, 12.7 mL, 12.7 mmol) was added. The resultant solution was
stirred for 8 h and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (EtOAc) to afford keto diol 9
(601 mg, 84%) as a colorless oil: keto diol 9, yield 601 mg, 84% [α]D25
+5.6 (c 0.5, CHCl3); IR (film) 3399, 1711, 1457, 1377, 1171 cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.00 (1H, d, J = 11.5 Hz), 3.87 (1H, dd, J = 12.0, 1.5
Hz), 3.56 (1H, d, J = 12.0 Hz), 3.54 (1H, dd, J = 11.5, 4.5 Hz), 2.71
(1H, dd, J = 15.5, 12.0 Hz), 2.52 (1H, dd, J = 17.0, 2.5 Hz), 2.49 (1H,
dd, J = 17.0, 2.5 Hz), 2.36-2.30 (2H, m), 2.15-2.11 (1H, m), 1.95-1.84
(2H, m); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 212.0, 80.6, 71.9, 63.8, 62.1, 43.7,
41.0, 39.8, 37.5, 33.2, 25.6; HRMS (ESI TOF) calcd for C11H16O3Na [M+Na]+
219.0992 found 219.0999.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Simple, Efficient, and Enantiocontrolled Synthesis of a Near-Structural
Mimic of Platensimycin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yeung, Ying-Yeung; Corey, E. J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(17), 3877-3878

