$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Potassium 4-Hydroxyethylphenyltrifluoroborate (3a). 4-
Acetylphenylboronic acid (1.00 g, 6.10 mmol) was dissolved in anhyd EtOH
(5.0 mL) and cooled 0 °C with an ice/water bath. NaBH4 (579 mg, 15.2
mmol) was added all at once as a solid. After stirring for 16 h,
additional EtOH (5.0 mL) was added and the mixture was stirred for 4 h.
The soln was cooled to 0 °C and treated with 1N HCl (30 mL, 30 mmol). The
mixture was then extracted with EtOAc (3 X 15 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and
concentrated. The crude boronic acid was then dissolved in MeOH (10 mL)
and cooled to 0 °C. Satd aq KHF2 (6.8 mL, 31 mmol) was added dropwise via
syringe. The mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 2 h, concentrated, and
placed under high-vacuum (0.001 Torr) for 3 h. The dried solids were
triturated with hot acetone (3 X 20 mL) and filtered to remove
inorganicsalts. The resulting filtrate was concentrated and Et2O was
added to precipitate a white solid (1.15 g, 83%): Potassium
4-Hydroxyethylphenyltrifluoroborate (3a). , yield (1.15 g, 83%): mp >210
°C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.26 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H) 7.05 (d, J = 7.6
Hz, 2H), 4.85 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 1H), 4.63-4.59 (m, 1H), 1.28 (d, J = 6.4
Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, DMSO- d6) δ 143.6, 130.9, 123.3, 68.5, 26.0;
11B NMR (128 MHz, DMSO- d6) δ 2.30 (br s); 19F NMR (471 MHz, DMSO- d6) δ
-139.2 (m); IR (KBr) 3368, 2973, 2875, 1610 cm- 1; HRMS calcd. for
C8H9BF3O [M-K]- 189.0698, found 189.0704.
