$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Transformation of C-B bond to hydroxy group;
(1R*,2R*)-2-[(1S*,2S*)-1,4-Dimethyl-2-hydroxypentyl]-1-cycloheptanol
(21). A solution of the ketone 20 (0.180 g, 0.54 mmol, 90% ds) in
methanol was slowly added to 5% palladium on carbon (0.5 g) under
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction vessel was put in an autoclave and then
pressurized with hydrogen (20 atm). After 2 h, hydrogen was released. The
reaction mixture was filtered with a pad of Florisil® by using Et2O as an
eluent. After removal of methanol in vacuo, BH3·THF (1.0 M in THF, 1.6
mL, 1.6 mmol) was added to the crude product at -78°C. The reaction
mixture was gradually warmed to 0°C and stirred for 3 h at that
temperature. THF and unreacted BH 3 were removed in vacuo. Methanol (5.0
mL) and 30% aqueous H2O2 (1.0 mL) were added in tern at 0 °C. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 1 h. Saturated
aqueous Na2S2O3 (5.0 mL) was slowly added at 0°C. Methanol was removed in
vacuo, and then the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O five times. The
combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, and filtrated. The solvents were removed in vacuo. The resulting
crude product was purified with column chromatography on silica gel (30,
50% Et2O in hexane) to give the title compound (0.099 g, 81% yield, 85%
ds determined by 1H NMR analysis) as a colorless liquid. Rf = 0.14 (20%
AcOEt in hexane); IR (neat) 3330 (br, O-H), 1729, 1260 and 1044 (C-O),
972; 1H NMR δ 0.91 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H, CH(CH3)CH3), 0.92 (d, J= 6.8 Hz,
3H, CH(CH3)CH3), 0.97 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H, CHCH3), 1.19-1.86 (m, 15H, CHCH2
CH(OH)CH(CH3)CH(CH2)5 ),3.90 (dd, J= 4.2, 8.8 Hz, 1H, (CH2)5CHOH),
4.14-4.20 (m, 1H, CH(CH3)CHOH); 13C NMR δ 10.5, 22.9, 22.3, 23.4, 24.9,
25.0, 28.2, 28.6, 36.6, 41.7, 45.1, 47.0, 71.3, 71.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
