$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Asymmetric Reduction of Acetophenone with
Catalyst 2; Typical Procedure. A 100 mL, flame-dried, two-necked,
round-bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirrer bar was charged
with catalyst 2 (0.66 mmol) and anhyd THF (4 mL). PhCOMe (2 mmol, 0.22
mL) was then added under argon from a syringe. Subsequently, BH3•THF (2.4
mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added dropwise with the aid of a syringe pump at a
rate of 1 mL/h, and the solution was then stirred at r.t. under argon for
18 h. When the reaction was complete, the mixture was hydrolyzed by
addition of MeOH (5 mL) and 1 M aq HCl (5 mL). Workup as described in
ref. 14 gave enantiomerically enriched 1-phenylethanol as a colorless
oil; yield: 0.19 g (78%). (1S)-1,2,3,4-Tetrahydronaphth-1-ol (4c) 16. ee
46% (catalyst B). HPLC: Lux Cellulose-1, hexane-i-PrOH (95:5); flow rate:
1.0 mL/min, λ = 254 nm; tR (S) = 9.8 min, tR (R) = 10.7 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 46% ee, alternatively reaction carried out using
(2R)-2-amino-2-phenylethanol N-borane catalyst decreased yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic asymmetric reduction of prochiral ketones with chiral β-amino
alcohol N-boranes and the corresponding tris(oxazaborolidine)borazines
