$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of ketone 9 (81.5 mg, 0.367 mmol) and methanol (3.67 mL)
cooled to 0 °C was added CeCl3.7H2O (164 mg, 0.44 mmol). The reaction was
stirred at 0 °C for 5 min then NaBH4 (27.7 mg, 0.734 mmol) was added and
allowed to stir at 0 °C for 30 min. The reaction was quenched with
aqueous HCl (2 mL, 1 M) and warmed to room temperature. The reaction was
allowed to stir for another 30 min at room temperature and diluted with
Et2O (6 mL) after the deprotection was deemed complete by TLC analysis.
The organic layer was washed with brine (5 mL) and dried with MgSO4.
Product was purified through a short silica gel plug (3 cm) to give enone
10 (53 mg, 80%) as a clear oil. 2-(1-hydroxyhex-5-enyl)cyclopent-2-enone
(10). Rf 0.17 (pentane:Et2O 3:2); 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.45 (td, 1H,
J = 2.8, 1.2 Hz), 5.80 (ddt, 1H, J = 16.8, 10.0, 6.8 Hz), 4.98 (m, 2H),
4.45 (m, 1H), 2.78 (br s, 1H, O-H) 2.61 (m, 2H), 2.45 (m, 2H), 2.10 (m,
2H), 1.68 (m, 2H), 1.57 (m, 1H), 1.46 (m, 1H). 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ
210.2, 158.2, 148.1, 138.9, 115.2, 68.2, 35.9, 35.8, 34.1, 27.2, 25.4. IR
(NaCl, thin film) 3463 (br), 2947 (m), 2862 (m), 1693 (s), 1638 (m), 1439
(m), 1000 (m) cm-1. HRMS (M + Na) C11H16O2Na Calcd: 203.1048. Found:
203.1044.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solvent-controlled intramolecular [2 + 2] photocycloadditions of
α-substituted enones
