$DATUM (1R,2R,3S,4S)-(+)-3-Amino-1,7,7-trimethylbicyclo[2.2.1]heptan-2-ol (19):
21 (3.07 g, 92%), which was immediately dissolved in anhyd Et2O (50 mL)
and added dropwise at 0 °C to a suspension of LiAlH4 (1.90 g, 50 mmol) in
anhyd Et2O (100 mL). The mixture was stirred at r.t. for 18 h, then
cooled to 0 °C and aq 10% NaOH (2 mL) was slowly added. The mixture was
stirred at r.t. for another 4 h, the precipitate was collected by
filtration. The precipitate was dissolved in Et2O by washing with Et2O (2
x 20 mL) and the combined Et2O layers were dried (MgSO4). Et2O was
removed to afford the desired amino alcohol as a mixture of stereoisomers
19 and 23 (95:5) and traces of 24. Yield 2.47 g, 73%. mp 161.5-163 °C
(Lit. mp 163 °C); [α]25D +37.8 (c 1.00, MeOH) (Lit. [α]25D +36.0 (c 1.04,
MeOH). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.86 (s, 3 H, CH3), 0.89 (s, 6 H,
2CH3), 1.07-1.17 (m, 1 H, CH2), 1.33-1.52 (m, 2 H, CH2), 1.70 (t, J = 4.2
Hz, 1 H, CH), 1.71-1.82 (m, 1 H, CH2), 2.18 (br s, 3 H, OH, NH2), 3.49
(dd, J = 8.7, 4.2 Hz, 1 H, CH), 3.35 (dd, J = 8.7, 1.5 Hz, 1 H, CH). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = (CH3), 18.29 (CH3), 18.39 (CH2), 19.98 (CH3),
25.47 (CH2), 45.21 (C), 48.48 (CH), 49.42 (C), 50.70 (CH), 72.87 (CH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 95:5 cis:trans, dropwise addition of reactant in stage 1
substage 1, slow addition of reagent in stage 2 substage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric reduction of α-keto aldoxime O-ethers
