$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reduction of α-Keto Aldoxime O-Ethers with Borane/Oxazaborolidine;
General Procedure : To a solution of the appropriate amino alcohol (2
mmol) in THF (10 mL) was added 10 M BMS (borane-methyl sulfide complex)
(0.2 mL, 2 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at r.t. for 1 h. THF (5 mL)
and the rest of BMS (0.8 mL, 8 mmol) were added and the mixture was
stirred for another 10 min. The mixture was cooled to 0 °C and α-keto
aldoxime ether (2 mmol) in THF (15 mL) was added in 2.5 h using a syringe
pump. The mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 10 min, at r.t. for 30 min, and
refluxed for 18 h. After cooling to r.t., aq 3 M HCl (12 mL) was added
slowly and the mixture was allowed to stir for 5 h. THF was removed on a
rotary evaporator; then EtOAc (30 mL) and NaCl (5 g) were added to the
residue, and the mixture was basified with aq 10% NaOH to pH 12 and
stirred for 5 min. The organic layer was separated and the residue was
extracted with EtOAc (5 x 15 mL). The combined organic extracts were
dried (MgSO4). The solvent was removed and the product was isolated by
flash chromatography on silica gel (CH2Cl2-MeOH, 90:10). The product was
derivatized with trifluoroacetic anhydride in the presence of Et3N and
analyzed by GC on a chiral β-Dex 325 capillary column (30 m x 0.25 mm).
Commercially available chiral 2-amino-1-phenylethanols were also
derivatized with trifluoroacetic anhydride and analyzed by GC as
comparative samples. Yield 72%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, incremental addition of reagent in stage 1 substage 1,
slow addition of reagent in stage 3 substage 1, alternative reaction
conditions gave lower yield, 46% ee, product depends on reaction
temperature and time, slow addition of reactant in stage 2 substage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric reduction of α-keto aldoxime O-ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bosiak, Mariusz J.; Pakulski, Marcin M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (2), 316-324

